    "legend_note": "BD CARTO® V5, everything 5 m wide and over — 250,653 segments. Line weight is the width class, not a measurement: BD CARTO records width in four buckets. Blue is natural watercourse, teal is canal, violet marks where the network is traced through a reservoir, lake or marsh rather than flowing. Every width class is drawn at every zoom, so the whole network shows with all of France in view. Lakes are filled areas beneath the lines — blue for natural lakes, ponds and lagoons, teal for reservoirs, gravel pits and basins, which are built and can be drawn down. Lakes over 1 km² show from the national view; smaller ones appear as you zoom in, down to the farm pond."
